摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Composable mathematics tools for agents","id":"gh:1309745037","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"jacobian","slug":"morluto/jacobian","topics":["ai-agents","automated-theorem-proving","computer-algebra","cordis","dsh","dsh-plugin","erdos","erdos-problem","formal-methods","formal-verification","lean4","math","mcp","mcp-server","model-context-protocol","proof-assistant","python","symbolic-math","sympy","theorem-proving"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Composable mathematics tools for agents"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**English** · 简体中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Jacobian"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"An executable mathematical vocabulary for agents: discover one typed operation, run it, and compose "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"le mathematical vocabulary for agents: discover one typed operation, run it, and compose its result."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Jacobian is an MCP server that gives AI agents a searchable vocabulary of typed\nmathematical operati"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ons. `math.find` matches a mathematical need or inspects one\nexact contract, and `math.run` executes"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" it and returns its typed result. The same\nmathematical library is also available through a CLI and "},{"id":"p5s4","text":"s typed result. The same\nmathematical library is also available through a CLI and native Python API."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Each operation establishes one stable, reusable mathematical postcondition\nrather than prescribing a"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" workflow or proof strategy. Results are exact where\nclaimed and make approximation, incompleteness,"},{"id":"p6s3","text":" or uncertainty explicit."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"**Jacobian's hypothesis is that mathematical reasoning benefits from an\nexecutable vocabulary of sem"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"antically scoped, bounded operations.** Rather than\nexposing large domain solvers or precomposed wor"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"kflows, Jacobian exposes\nmathematical primitives that agents can search for and compose into solutio"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ns\nbeyond what any individual operation was designed to solve. The library\nsupplies trustworthy math"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"ematical moves; the reasoning model decides which\nmoves to make, how to combine their results, and w"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"hen to stop. Keeping the\noperations semantically narrow and domain-owned preserves that search space"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"\ninstead of baking one proof strategy or workflow into the tools themselves."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"See Executable mathematical vocabulary\nfor what semantic atomicity means and how the operation vocab"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"le mathematical vocabulary\nfor what semantic atomicity means and how the operation vocabulary grows."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Quickstart"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Set up Jacobian for your agents with a single command. The setup command\nrequires Node.js 20.17+, 22"},{"id":"p10s2","text":".13+, or 23.5+ and `uvx` on your `PATH`."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Choose detected agents and review the changes before they are written. Setup\ndoes not install Node.j"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"s, Python, `uv`, or an agent. For automation, preview\nan explicit plan with `npx jacobian@latest set"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"up --codex --dry-run`; use\n`--yes` only with explicit agent flags or `--all`."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"To refresh an existing registration explicitly, run\n`npx jacobian@latest upgrade` and select the age"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"nts to update. The generated\nlauncher pins the exact release resolved by npm."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Run the canonical Python MCP command without installing Jacobian globally:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Where an MCP host requires an npm command, the npm package is a deterministic\ncarrier for that same "},{"id":"p16s2","text":" MCP host requires an npm command, the npm package is a deterministic\ncarrier for that same command:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"For a persistent installation:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"That package includes Jacobian's exact maintained Python backend stack: SymPy,\nNetworkX, Z3, and Pyt"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"hon-FLINT. A normal Python or npm installation\ntherefore exposes the same built-in Python-backed ope"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"ration portfolio. The\ntested binary-install contract is CPython 3.12 or 3.13 on glibc Linux x86-64;\n"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"the release gate installs the built wheel and starts Jacobian on both Python\nversions. Other systems"},{"id":"p20s5","text":" may have compatible upstream wheels, but are not part\nof the tested release contract yet. In partic"},{"id":"p20s6","text":"ular, Alpine/musl cannot install\nthe complete mandatory stack from PyPI."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Singular and QEPCAD are optional system runtimes for a small subset of operations.\nThe Python instal"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"lation does not provision them, and ordinary operations do not\nrequire Docker. Python callers can us"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"e `jacobian.backends.check_backend`; MCP\ninspection reports availability in the server environment. "},{"id":"p21s4","text":"See\nbackend requirements for exact coverage\nand setup."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The Python distribution contains the mathematical kernel, CLI, and MCP server.\nThe npm package deter"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ministically maps its exact package version to the\ncorresponding `uvx` invocation."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Compute one bounded result"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"An ordinary operation returns mathematics first. For example,\n`matrix.determinant.compute` accepts o"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ne exact rational matrix and returns its\ndeterminant directly. Callers compose results by passing th"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"eir typed values to a\nsubsequent operation."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"For a local terminal workflow, inspect the exact installed contract and run one\nof its examples with"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"al terminal workflow, inspect the exact installed contract and run one\nof its examples with the CLI:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The second command returns the gcd and Bézout coefficients as JSON. In an MCP\nhost, use `math.find` "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"in inspection mode to read the same contract and `math.run`\nwith the same payload shape. See Discove"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"r and invoke operations\nfor that agent workflow."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Available mathematics"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The built-in portfolio covers work in:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- polynomial maps and polynomial algebra;\n- exact linear algebra;\n- graphs, paths, colorings, and is"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"omorphism;\n- bounded SAT and SMT solving;\n- finite algebra, probability, geometry, and topology."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"SAT and SMT operations use the maintained Z3 Python binding directly. Use\n`math.find` to match the m"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"athematical result needed, then use its inspection\nmode on a promising operation before calling `mat"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"result needed, then use its inspection\nmode on a promising operation before calling `math.run` once."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"See the domain operation library\nfor the maintained operation portfolio and\nbackend requirements."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Status"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Jacobian 0.23.0  is pre-stable. Its published package and operation contracts\ndescribe the supported"},{"id":"p34s2","text":" surface; experimental operation contracts may change\nbetween releases."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"- Documentation home: tutorials, how-to guides, reference,\nand explanations\n- Architecture: runtime "},{"id":"p36s2","text":"structure and\ntrust boundaries\n- Product model: operation contracts,\nownership, and project boundari"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"es\n- Tool reference: MCP resources and invocation\ncontracts\n- Backend requirements:\nmaintained Pytho"},{"id":"p36s4","text":"n backends\n- Remote deployment: HTTP deployment and\nauthentication"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Contributing"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Jacobian uses Python 3.12, `uv`, and a small `Makefile`:"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"Read CONTRIBUTING.md before changing code. It documents\nfocused test commands, verification rules, d"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"ocumentation placement, and\npull-request expectations."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
